---
import ContentLayout from "../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SupportMatrix from "../components/data/SupportMatrix.astro";
import EvidenceLinks from "../components/data/EvidenceLinks.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Rooted in your desktop."
  eyebrow="Compatibility / Know your environment"
  description="Linux Mint, Cinnamon, Nemo and X11 are the primary tested combination. Other environments deserve specific answers, not a blanket Linux badge."
>
  <div class="content-split">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Availability isn’t verification.</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Recorded desktop testing</strong> means a named owner test is on
        record. <strong>Conditional</strong> means an implemented path has
        requirements or degradation. <strong>Manual verification needed</strong>{" "}
        means the code exists but the exact desktop was not certified.{" "}
        <strong>Unsupported</strong> identifies a missing shipping wheel or
        release target.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <h3>X11 is required for the wheel.</h3>
      <p>
        Native Wayland is unsupported. XWayland Invoke is experimental and
        conditional; Drag + Shift is unavailable in Wayland sessions. Exploring
        is a roadmap category, not a support promise.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={withBase("roadmap/")}>
        See what is being explored →
      </a>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="matrix-title">
    <h2 id="matrix-title">Find your environment.</h2>
    <SupportMatrix />
  </section>
  <div class="content-split">
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Compositing, monitors and scale.</h2>
      <p>
        Without a compositor, X11 uses an opaque/shaped Branching fallback.
        Concentric also falls back when its workarea or target sizes are
        insufficient. The default configuration reserves{" "}
        <strong>668 × 742 logical pixels</strong>; that is not a universal
        minimum for custom geometry.
      </p>
      <p>
        RandR and Xft scaling paths have automated coverage. Mixed-DPI monitors,
        hotplugging, negative origins and edge behavior still need
        environment-specific manual checks. N5’s outstanding cases remain
        visible despite later owner release sign-off.
      </p>
      <EvidenceLinks ids={["config", "n5", "x11-tests"]} />
    </section>
    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Check the feature, too.</h2>
      <p>
        Properties requires <code>org.freedesktop.FileManager1</code>. Clipboard
        Copy publishes X11 file URIs. Keyboard input during a foreign drag is
        best effort; use Invoke for keyboard-oriented navigation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Conversion supports static PNG/JPEG/WebP, not animation or arbitrary
        media formats. Runtime font availability affects Arabic/non-Latin text;
        widget containers remain LTR. Package installation does not prove GUI
        integration.
      </p>
      <EvidenceLinks ids={["actions", "doctor", "convert", "release-report"]} />
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="prose content-section">
    <h2>Help verify another desktop.</h2>
    <p>
      Report OS/version, desktop and window manager, X11/Wayland session,
      compositor, file manager/version, architecture, monitor layout and scale,
      Radivine version, and whether the package or a source build was used.
    </p>
    <p>
      With disposable files, record Drag + Shift and Invoke separately, submenu
      navigation, outside cancellation, clipboard/Properties, layout fallback
      and startup. Include expected versus actual behavior and redacted
      diagnostics. Do not mark an entire distribution supported from a single
      headless test.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href={withBase("contribute/")}>
      Prepare a useful test report →
    </a>
  </section>
  <nav class="page-links" aria-label="Related pages">
    <a href={withBase("download/")}>Download and installation →</a>
    <a href={withBase("guide/troubleshooting/")}>Troubleshoot your setup →</a>
  </nav>
</ContentLayout>
